Consider the following languages:
L_{1} = { a^{n}wa^{n} | w ∈ {a, b}* }
L_{2} = { wxwr | w, x ∈ {a, b}*, |w|, |x| > 0 }
Note that wr is the reversal of the string w. Which of the following is/are TRUE?

Consider the following languages:
L1 = {ww | w ∈ {a, b}* }
L2 = {a^{n}b^{n}c^{m}| m, n≥ 0}
L3 = {a^{m}b^{n}c^{n}| m, n≥ 0}
Which of the following statements is/are FALSE?

Consider the following languages.
L_{1}= {wxyx | w, x, y ε (0 + 1)^{+}}
L_{2}= {xy | x, y ε(a + b)*, |x| = |y|, x !=y}
Which one of the following is TRUE?

Consider the following languages:
L1 = {a^{n}b^{m}c^{n+m}: m, n > 1}
L2 = {a^{n}b^{n}c^{2n}: n > 1}
Which one of the following is TRUE?

Consider the following languages.
L1={a^{i}b^{j}c^{k}| i =j, k>=1}
L2={a^{i}b^{j}| j=2i , i >=0}
Which of the following is true?

